  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Futuremakers Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Phase two of a 3 year USD 3.3m SOYEE programme in 5 APAC countries funded by Standard Chartered Foundation. Working with local government, local vocational training colleges and 6000 young people (4,604 women) to facilitate skills building and employment readiness.  Also working with employers to facilitate gender equality in the workplace.  Programme Goal:  Young women access employment that is sustainable, gender transformative and disability inclusive.  * Please see project level for docs and reports*</narrative>
  </description>
